1
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:16,000
A story for everyone who works for a living.

2
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Glengarry Glen Ross is a crime, drama, mystery film directed by James Foley.

3
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Times are tough at Premiere Properties.

4
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:46,000
Shelley "the machine" Levene and Dave Moss are veteran
salesmen, but only Ricky Roma is on a hot streak.

5
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:56,000
The new Glengarry sales leads could turn everything around, but the front
office is holding them back until these "losers" prove themselves.

6
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Then someone decides to take matters into his own hands, stealing the
Glengarry leads and leaving everyone wondering who did it.

7
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:16,000
Ricky Roma, played by Al Pacino.

8
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Shelley Levene, played by Jack Lemmon.

9
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:36,000
Blake, played by Alec Baldwin.

10
00:41:40,000 --> 00:41:46,000
George Aaronow, played by Alan Arkin.

11
00:45:50,000 --> 00:45:56,000
Dave Moss, played by Ed Harris.

12
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
John Williamson, played by Kevin Spacey.

13
00:54:10,000 --> 00:54:16,000
Glengarry Glen Ross is a 1992 American dark comedy-drama film directed by James Foley and written
by David Mamet, based on his 1984 Pulitzer Prize–winning play of the same name.

14
00:58:20,000 --> 00:58:26,000
The film depicts two days in the lives of four real-estate salesmen and their increasing desperation when the corporate office
sends Blake, a motivational trainer with the threat that all but the top two salesmen will be fired within one week.

15
01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:36,000
Like the play, the film is notorious for its use of profanity, leading the cast
to refer to the film jokingly as Death of a Fuckin' Salesman.

16
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
The title of the film is derived from the names of two of the fictitious real-estate
developments being peddled by the salesmen: Glengarry Highlands and Glen Ross Farms.

17
01:10:50,000 --> 01:10:56,000
The film was critically acclaimed.

18
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
The world premiere was held at the 49th Venice Film Festival, where
Jack Lemmon was awarded the Volpi Cup for Best Actor.

19
01:19:10,000 --> 01:19:16,000
Al Pacino was nominated for an Academy Award and a Golden
Globe Award for Best Supporting Actor.

20
01:23:20,000 --> 01:23:26,000
However, the film was a box-office failure for grossing $10.7
million in North America against a $12.5 million budget.

21
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:36,000
It has since become a cult classic.

22
01:31:40,000 --> 01:31:46,000
The film explores themes of estate agent, robbery,
competition, office, dark comedy.

23
01:35:50,000 --> 01:35:56,000
The tone is mind_bending and dark and emotional.
